{
  "_comment": [
    "MezzoSopranoClef supports Minecraft versions in TWO distinct ways. Do not conflate them.",
    "",
    "1) `servers` \u2014 which SERVER versions the bot can join. One client build talks to all of them by",
    "   translating the protocol client-side with ViaFabricPlus. `status` here is filled in by",
    "   scripts/update_version_matrix.py from a real scripts/verify_versions.sh run:",
    "     verified  - a real vanilla server of this exact release was joined (tab list + screenshot)",
    "     expected  - shares a protocol with a verified neighbour; not itself run yet",
    "     failed    - the last matrix run could not join it (see `error`)",
    "   `serverJava` is the JDK major that release's vanilla server needs (for the test harness).",
    "",
    "2) `nativeClients` \u2014 which CLIENT versions have their own real mod build. This is what makes",
    "   VERSION-SPECIFIC MODS work: a 1.20.1 Fabric mod only loads next to a 1.20.1 build of the bot.",
    "   Protocol translation cannot provide this; each entry is a genuine port. `status`:",
    "     runtime-verified - booted and joined a real server of that version in this repo",
    "     jar-built        - compiles against that release and produces a remapped mod jar; not yet booted",
    "   `noGl` is whether that target can boot with NO OpenGL context at all. Where false the bot is",
    "   still headless (the world/GUI draw is skipped) but needs a real GL context \u2014 a hidden window,",
    "   or Xvfb/Mesa on a bare server \u2014 because that release has no stub-able Blaze3D device."
  ],
