  "nativeClientsNotStarted": {
    "forge": "No Forge target exists. Forge is a different loader again (its own entrypoints, event bus and build plugin). The loader seam that NeoForge proved out \u2014 ModPlatform plus a thin client wiring class over the shared ClefBotCore \u2014 is what a Forge port would reuse.",
    "1.12.2": "Forge-only, Java 8, and predates Mojang's published mappings (needs MCP/Parchment). The single largest port in the matrix; not attempted.",
    "fabric<=1.13.2": "1.14.4 is the floor: Mojang first published official mappings for it, and the whole matrix is built against Mojang mappings so common/ can be shared verbatim. Older releases would need a different mapping set (MCP/Parchment) and a separate toolchain.",
    "neoforge (other versions)": "Only 1.21.8 has a NeoForge target. Adding another NeoForge release is now a version bump like any other: reuse ClefBotCore and NeoForgePlatform, and port only that release's Minecraft glue.",
    "neoforge no-gl": "GPU-free (no-gl) booting is not implemented on NeoForge. NeoForge patches Blaze3D with its own extension interfaces (GpuDeviceExtension, plus extra RenderPass/CommandEncoder methods), so the vanilla-shaped stub device is not shareable. The NeoForge target runs headless behind a hidden window instead, exactly like the 1.21.4-and-older Fabric targets."
  }
}
